        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/03/eney-from-macpaw-ai-assistant-deep-apple-integrations/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/10/Banners-AI-Assistant-Dark.png?w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">MacPaw, the makers of CleanMyMac and Setapp, have <a href=\"https://bit.ly/4A8yVPt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener sponsored nofollow\">an AI assistant called Eney</a> that’s designed for Apple users. Eney is available across Mac and iPhone and is built to integrate with core Apple services like Mail, Calendar, and Reminders, plus a lot more.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1076532\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/03/eney-from-macpaw-ai-assistant-deep-apple-integrations/#more-1076532\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
