        "title": "iPhone 18 will have two upgrades inspired by ‘Pro’ models, per leak",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/03/iphone-18-will-have-two-upgrades-inspired-by-pro-models-per-leak/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/ios-26-5-pride-luminance-iphone-17-pro-black.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple has <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/09/no-iphone-18-announced-today-heres-why/\" data-type=\"post\" data-id=\"1067979\">yet to launch</a> the iPhone 18, with only 18 Pro and Duo models debuting this fall. But a new leak points to two iPhone 18 upgrades that will follow the pattern of the iPhone 18 Pro.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"iphone,iphone-18\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1077219\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/03/iphone-18-will-have-two-upgrades-inspired-by-pro-models-per-leak/#more-1077219\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
        "source": "9to5Mac"
