        "title": "T-Mobile launches 5-gigabit fiber for $90/mo with 10-year price guarantee",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/03/t-mobile-launches-5-gigabit-fiber-for-90-mo-with-10-year-price-guarantee/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/11/T-Mobile-launches-5-gigabit-fiber-for-90mo-with-10-year-price-guarantee.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/t-mobile/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">T-Mobile</a> has announced a new 5 gigabit fiber broadband service priced at $90 a month, starting today. The company also says that if you sign up now, the price is guaranteed not to increase for a full decade … </p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"t-mobile,tech-industry\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1077179\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/03/t-mobile-launches-5-gigabit-fiber-for-90-mo-with-10-year-price-guarantee/#more-1077179\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
